FunctieVivaldis Office is looking for a Customer Service Officer for our client in Hasselt. Our client is specialised in incident management and roadside assistance.Feel free to take a look at the vacancy! If you have any questions, you can reach us by phone on  3211 94 81 56.Your duties as a customer service officer will include:
• You'll respond to incoming phone calls and mails;
• You'll gather the necessary information and check it's accuracy and completeness;
• You'll provide the needed technical support and communicate with the workshops;
• You'll update all the involved parties;
• You'll monitor the agreements;
• You'll follow the contract-related issues up and respect the imposed deadlines.Profiel
As a customer service officer you can recognise yourself in the criteria below:

• Preferably you have gained a first experience in customer service;
• You can easily work with the computer, especially with MS Office;
• You're a social person with strong communication skills;
• You have attention to detail and are stress-resistant;
• You work organised and have great organizational and time management skills;
• You must speak fluently Dutch/Polish/English OR Polish/ German/ English OR English/German/Dutch OR French/ German/ English
• You work the weekend   Friday shift OR during the week. You work 40 hours/ week between 07.00-22.00h.Wat je van ons krijgt
What's in it for you as the new customer service officer:

• You'll end up in a leading company in an international environment;
• You'll work in a full-time position with a strong emphasis on work-life balance;
• You'll receive a competitive salary including meal vouchers worth €7 and eco-vouchers;
• The company hosts various social events to boost the team spirit;
• Hard work pays off! After a successful interim period you'll receive a permanent contract.
We look forward to your application if you're convinced of this vacancy.

.

Our client is a leading international trading and supply chain organization with a long-established presence across Europe and a strong global footprint. Active in the distribution and trading of industrial and chemical products, the company combines commercial expertise, logistics capabilities, and financial strength to support international business operations.

Jobomschrijving

As Senior Accountant, you will play a key role in ensuring the accuracy of accounting operations, compliance, and financial reporting within an international business environment. Working closely with a Shared Service Center and stakeholders across Europe, your responsibilities will include:

• Managing monthly, quarterly, and annual closing activities, including accruals, reconciliations, and balance sheet reviews;
• Acting as the accounting reference point for the Belgian entity and overseeing the quality of accounting transactions processed by the Shared Service Center;
• Taking ownership of VAT compliance, tax-related reporting, and statutory obligations across multiple European jurisdictions;
• Coordinating annual audits and supporting the preparation of statutory financial statements;
• Partnering with business teams to provide accounting and tax guidance on commercial and operational activities;
• Ensuring compliance with local regulations, internal controls, and group accounting policies;
• Identifying opportunities to streamline processes, strengthen controls, and drive continuous improvement initiatives;
• Contributing to digitization and automation projects, including the adoption of innovative technologies and AI-driven solutions;

We are looking for a collaborative and flexible professional who enjoys taking ownership and working in a team-oriented environment. The ideal candidate combines technical accounting expertise with a strong process improvement mindset and has an interest in digital transformation and emerging technologies such as AI.

• Bachelor's degree in Accounting, Finance, or a related field;
• Minimum 4 years of accounting experience within an international or B2B environment;
• Strong understanding of Belgian GAAP and VAT regulations;
• Experience with statutory accounting and external audits;
• Knowledge of SAP S/4HANA or SAP Hana is considered a strong asset;
• Fluent in English and French; Dutch is a plus;
• Analytical, detail-oriented, and process-minded;
• Comfortable working with multiple stakeholders in an international environment;
• Proactive, hands-on, and eager to contribute to continuous improvement initiatives;

Robert Half is currently looking for a Receptionist (m/f/x).

The company is located in Brussels and this is a full-time position within a legal services environment.

The responsibilities of this position as Receptionist are:

• Welcoming clients, visitors and business partners in a professional and courteous manner;
• Managing incoming calls and ensuring enquiries are efficiently directed to the appropriate person;
• Preparing meeting rooms and contributing to a smooth, welcoming and professional client experience;
• Coordinating incoming and outgoing mail, courier services and deliveries;
• Providing administrative support, including document handling, filing, archiving and printing;
• Monitoring office supplies and liaising with suppliers when necessary;
• Helping maintain an organised, professional and pleasant working environment;
• Providing practical support to colleagues and contributing to the efficient day-to-day running of the office;
• Working closely with the morning receptionist to ensure continuity throughout the day and foster good collaboration within the team.


The required qualifications for this position as Receptionist are:

• You have a very good command of Dutch, French and English;
• You have a good knowledge of Office 365;
• You are customer-oriented and enjoy interacting with different people;
• You take ownership and proactively look for solutions;
• You are organised and have a strong eye for detail;
• You remain calm and efficient when priorities change;
• You are reliable, discreet and professional;
• You enjoy working in a dynamic environment and are a strong team player.
